// endpoint_set_keepalive.proto — SetKeepalive: hold the session's keep-alive
// cadence, or let it run again. SESSION section.
//
// A HIDDEN WORKSPACE'S CACHE IS LEFT TO LAPSE, NOT STOOD DOWN AT ONCE
// (owner request, 2026-10-13). When the user hides a workspace the daemon
// HOLDS its keep-alives: the shim sends no further keep-alive, so the prompt
// cache lapses on its own clock, and the user still has until that moment to
// show the workspace again with its cache warm. While held, the shim states
// the projected lapse on the session stream (conversation.v1.SessionCacheLapse)
// so the daemon can count it down and stand the session down when it comes.
// Showing the workspace again RUNS the cadence, which schedules from the
// conversation's last request exactly as a session start does.
//
// A session can also be BORN held: StartSessionRequest.hold_keepalive, so a
// hidden workspace's session started by anything (a rollout's restart, a
// prompt) never sends a keep-alive between its start and a later hold.

